   "i": "Goods that are hard to come by trip up a man's conduct.",
   "n": "難得之貨 came already in chapter 3 (不貴難得之貨) and will come again: 之 turns the verb phrase 難得 'hard to get' into a modifier, so the whole thing is one noun, 'hard-to-get goods'. 行 is the same character as 'to walk'; here it is walking taken as a life — conduct, how a man carries himself — so the line is not only about theft but about being knocked off one's path."
